      "Inspected all 14 current portable frames: lit preview, four turntable views and nine named close/silhouette views. The through-gate is open, north and south arcades have the documented different counts, clocks face outward, lower and upper glazing remains visible, and the nine-bell belfry is genuinely open.",
      "Corrected the eastern loggia from an open decorative shell to the solid curved gable visible in the Museum of Moscow 1930 photograph. Rechecked the two-flight uncovered stair, carved surrounds, narrow diagonal shaft windows, four small tents, bare finial and rainwater pipes. No remaining visible inverted faces, covered apertures, detached trim or clipping defects were found."
